1
00:00:03.453 --> 00:00:08.505
Inspections assigned to you are under To
do — you also get an email when one is

2
00:00:08.505 --> 00:00:10.005
booked.

3
00:00:11.188 --> 00:00:16.372
At the top: the tenant's phone, ID number
and emergency contact — what you need on

4
00:00:16.372 --> 00:00:17.872
site.

5
00:00:17.872 --> 00:00:22.805
Go room by room. A tick means the room is
rated and has its three photos.

6
00:00:25.585 --> 00:00:29.585
On a move-out, every feature shows how it
was at move-in.

7
00:00:39.224 --> 00:00:44.224
Rate each feature. Something wrong? Mark
it, say what, and photograph it.

8
00:00:49.456 --> 00:00:54.438
At least three photos per room — they
protect you and the tenant if there's a

9
00:00:54.438 --> 00:00:55.938
dispute.

10
00:01:00.604 --> 00:01:05.104
Take the final meter readings — the
manager's checkout uses them.

11
00:01:08.559 --> 00:01:11.559
Count the keys the tenant hands back.

12
00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:27.119
The tenant signs on your phone. Not there,
or won't sign? Record that instead and

13
00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:28.619
carry on.

14
00:01:28.844 --> 00:01:33.838
Hand it in. Your findings lock — the
manager reviews them but can't change what

15
00:01:33.838 --> 00:01:35.338
you saw.

16
00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:41.159
The manager is emailed, prices any damage
and raises the repair jobs.

17
00:01:41.161 --> 00:01:44.661
That's an inspection: room by room,
photos, sign-off, hand in.
